  "claim": "The first Russian composer to make a lasting impression internationally was Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky not the composer of L'honesta negli amori.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Alessandro Scarlatti. Sentence: Pietro Alessandro Gaspare Scarlatti (2 May 1660 – 22 October 1725) was an Italian Baroque composer, especially famous for his operas and chamber cantatas.\nPage: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky. Sentence: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky ( ; Russian: Пётр Ильи́ч Чайко́вский ; 25 April/7 May 1840 – 25 October/6 November 1893), often anglicized as Peter Ilich Tchaikovsky, was a Russian composer of the romantic period, some of whose works are among the most popular music in the classical repertoire.\nPage: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky. Sentence: He was the first Russian composer whose music made a lasting impression internationally, bolstered by his appearances as a guest conductor in Europe and the United States.\nPage: L'honestà negli amori. Sentence: L'honestà negli amori is a dramma per musica in 3 acts by composer Alessandro Scarlatti.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Alessandro Scarlatti. Sentence: Pietro Alessandro Gaspare Scarlatti (2 May 1660 – 22 October 1725) was an Italian Baroque composer, especially famous for his operas and chamber cantatas.\nPage: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky. Sentence: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky ( ; Russian: Пётр Ильи́ч Чайко́вский ; 25 April/7 May 1840 – 25 October/6 November 1893), often anglicized as Peter Ilich Tchaikovsky, was a Russian composer of the romantic period, some of whose works are among the most popular music in the classical repertoire.\nPage: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky. Sentence: He was the first Russian composer whose music made a lasting impression internationally, bolstered by his appearances as a guest conductor in Europe and the United States.\nPage: L'honestà negli amori. Sentence: L'honestà negli amori is a dramma per musica in 3 acts by composer Alessandro Scarlatti.",
