        "original_id": "cb7b1d58-691b-5c7e-8fa1-ba97364977ff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alessandro Scarlatti, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky\n- Works: L'honestà negli amori\n- Topics: Baroque music, Romantic music, opera, chamber cantatas, international reputation\n\nFacts:\n- Alessandro Scarlatti was an Italian Baroque composer who lived from 2 May 1660 to 22 October 1725.\n- Alessandro Scarlatti was especially famous for his operas and chamber cantatas.\n- L'honestà negli amori is a dramma per musica in three acts by Alessandro Scarlatti.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was a Russian composer of the Romantic period who lived from 25 April/7 May 1840 to 25 October/6 November 1893.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was often anglicized as Peter Ilich Tchaikovsky.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky composed works that are among the most popular music in the classical repertoire.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was the first Russian composer whose music made a lasting international impression.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky’s international reputation was bolstered by his appearances as a guest conductor in Europe and the United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
